<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Council of India</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1858–1937</span> · Also known as India Council</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> was a body in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> that advised the Secretary of State for India from 1858 to 1937. Created by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/government-of-india-act-1858">Government of India Act 1858</a>, it was made up mainly of men with long experience of India, and its approval was needed for spending from Indian revenues. Its role was reduced over time, and it was abolished when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/government-of-india-act-1935">Government of India Act 1935</a> came into force.</p></div>
